{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1526281-personalized-instruments-and-conjunctional-sphere-effects","id":1526281,"title":"Personalized Instruments and Conjunctional Sphere Effects","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-12-03T11:42:51-08:00","id":1526281,"title":"Personalized Instruments and Conjunctional Sphere Effects","content":"I've been puttering around on a Mage character concept for a little while now, and I recently ran into a question that I couldn't find an answer to after a bit of searching online. While it's already implied, I'm talking M20 rules specifically.<br /> <br /> A Mage that uses a Personalized Instrument in order to cast an Effect with their Affinity Sphere receives -1 to the Difficulty on the Arete roll. So obviously that covers anything which only uses the Mind Sphere.<br /> <br /> But then I started pondering some ideas for Rotes that I've been working on, and I started to wonder how about how a Personalized Instrument might interact with Effects involving multiple Spheres. I'm going to use the Rotes as examples to help demonstrate my thoughts on different cases.<br /> <br /> (I'm also pretty inexperienced when it comes to designing Mage Effects, so let me know if I'm on the wrong track with anything!)<br /> <br /> So my first example would be a Correspondence 2 scrying spell which also includes Mind 1 to allow the Mage to pay full attention simultaneously to his everyday life and whatever is being observed by magic. In this case, the Mind Sphere is only serving to augment what is primarily a Correspondence Effect.<br /> <br /> My second example is a Correspondence 2 / Mind 2 &quot;Slipstream&quot;-type Effect which combines subtle warps of space and perception to increase the Difficulty of attack rolls, combining two different kinds of defence to make it still somewhat effective against an opponent who could resist either Effect on its own. In this case, you have two separate Spheres working towards a particular function, but using largely distinct methods of contributing to that outcome.<br /> <br /> If the Mage in question had Mind as their Affinity Sphere, would they receive a -1 Difficulty on their Arete roll for using a Personalized Instrument?<br /> <br /> The first example seems the most likely to be No, since you're just kind of &quot;splashing&quot; Mind in to beef up another Sphere's Effect.<br /> <br /> The second example seems more of a Maybe, since you do have a &quot;full&quot; Mind Effect as part of the function of the spell.<br /> <br /> My intuition is that it depends on whether or not the &quot;main&quot; Effect or function lies within the purview of the Affinity Sphere, but I feel like that could get messy. And, again, I have less experience with this stuff, so I figured I'd get some feedback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-05T23:51:32-08:00","id":1526390,"title":"","content":"In M20 instruments are not tied to Spheres. If you can incorporate a personalised instrument into your Effect, you get the -1 difficulty break. The main mechanical consequence of an Affinity Sphere is that it costs less experience points to increase.<br /> <br /> Also, those are cool rote ideas <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-06T09:38:07-08:00","id":1526408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thebian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1526281-personalized-instruments-and-conjunctional-sphere-effects?p=1526390#post1526390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In M20 instruments are not tied to Spheres. If you can incorporate a personalised instrument into your Effect, you get the -1 difficulty break. The main mechanical consequence of an Affinity Sphere is that it costs less experience points to increase.<br /> <br /> Also, those are cool rote ideas <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the feed-back on the rotes! I am kind of wondering if the &quot;Slipstream&quot; effect may be a bit Vulgar, or at least might trigger the Domino Effect if overused? Considering a 1-dot version that's more just &quot;Correspondence for &quot;eyes-in-the-back-of-your-head&quot; + Mind to focus that perception on hostiles.&quot;<br /> <br /> Regarding Personalized Instruments, p.587 of M20 Core does specify that the -1 Difficulty modifier from Personalized Instruments only applies to the Affinity Sphere.<br /> <br /> But setting aside the simple rotes like these, I wonder how that applies to complex Effects like creating a fully-functional human out of nothing. Clearly you need powerful applications of the Mind Sphere in order to create mind out of nothing for your new person, but that is ultimately just one portion of the smorgasbord of Sphere knowledge required to pull off such a feat. It then creates a weird situation where it becomes EASIER to create complex life-form *with* a mind if you allow the bonus to apply under those circumstances.<br /> <br /> Thank you very much for the response!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 12-06-2023, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T10:35:15-08:00","id":1526607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thebian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1526281-personalized-instruments-and-conjunctional-sphere-effects?p=1526390#post1526390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In M20 instruments are not tied to Spheres. If you can incorporate a personalised instrument into your Effect, you get the -1 difficulty break. The main mechanical consequence of an Affinity Sphere is that it costs less experience points to increase.<br /> <br /> Also, those are cool rote ideas <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is true except for personalised instruments which do indeed provide the -1 diff on effects which involve their affinity sphere:<br /> <br /> &quot;Certain mages employ personalised or unique tools - a lucky baseball, rowan wand, hand-built guitar, and so forth. Such personalised instruments resonate with the mage who employs them. There is, perhaps, a touch of Resonance between such symbols and an individual character. In game terms, a personal tool reflects that character's connection to a sphere - a bridge between artist and Art.<br /> For your character's affinity sphere (as described in chapter six), choose one personal instrument that fits his practice with that sphere. AProgenitor Genegineer might connect to Life through a mutagennic cocktail of chemicals, whereas a Bata's houngan unites himself with the same Sphere through a gift of whiskey, three cigars, and a virgin for Baron Samedi. The personal tool represents your mage's original training and connection with the Sphere in question. In return for sticking close to your roots, you can reduce by -1 the difficulty of a roll that employs that Sphere.<br /> <br /> M20 Pg587<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T10:39:17-08:00","id":1526608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1526281-personalized-instruments-and-conjunctional-sphere-effects#post1526281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been puttering around on a Mage character concept for a little while now, and I recently ran into a question that I couldn't find an answer to after a bit of searching online. While it's already implied, I'm talking M20 rules specifically.<br /> <br /> A Mage that uses a Personalized Instrument in order to cast an Effect with their Affinity Sphere receives -1 to the Difficulty on the Arete roll. So obviously that covers anything which only uses the Mind Sphere.<br /> <br /> But then I started pondering some ideas for Rotes that I've been working on, and I started to wonder how about how a Personalized Instrument might interact with Effects involving multiple Spheres. I'm going to use the Rotes as examples to help demonstrate my thoughts on different cases.<br /> <br /> (I'm also pretty inexperienced when it comes to designing Mage Effects, so let me know if I'm on the wrong track with anything!)<br /> <br /> So my first example would be a Correspondence 2 scrying spell which also includes Mind 1 to allow the Mage to pay full attention simultaneously to his everyday life and whatever is being observed by magic. In this case, the Mind Sphere is only serving to augment what is primarily a Correspondence Effect.<br /> <br /> My second example is a Correspondence 2 / Mind 2 &quot;Slipstream&quot;-type Effect which combines subtle warps of space and perception to increase the Difficulty of attack rolls, combining two different kinds of defence to make it still somewhat effective against an opponent who could resist either Effect on its own. In this case, you have two separate Spheres working towards a particular function, but using largely distinct methods of contributing to that outcome.<br /> <br /> If the Mage in question had Mind as their Affinity Sphere, would they receive a -1 Difficulty on their Arete roll for using a Personalized Instrument?<br /> <br /> The first example seems the most likely to be No, since you're just kind of &quot;splashing&quot; Mind in to beef up another Sphere's Effect.<br /> <br /> The second example seems more of a Maybe, since you do have a &quot;full&quot; Mind Effect as part of the function of the spell.<br /> <br /> My intuition is that it depends on whether or not the &quot;main&quot; Effect or function lies within the purview of the Affinity Sphere, but I feel like that could get messy. And, again, I have less experience with this stuff, so I figured I'd get some feedback.</div> </div> </div> </div>The answer is that this is very much up to the ST how far the personalised instrument can be pushed. Considering the in text description states the bonus is for sticking close to your roots, I think the answer would depend on whether those uses of the instrument were part of your mage's practice in training, or if they were a new innovation.<br /> <br /> I would agree that if you are just adding Mind to get the -1 diff, that would be pretty game mechanic-y and might be subject to scrutiny, but some STs are as simple as (hey, if your character believes their personal instrument is helping them with this, then they get the -1)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-11T20:49:01-08:00","id":1526690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1526281-personalized-instruments-and-conjunctional-sphere-effects#post1526281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been puttering around on a Mage character concept for a little while now, and I recently ran into a question that I couldn't find an answer to after a bit of searching online. While it's already implied, I'm talking M20 rules specifically.<br /> <br /> A Mage that uses a Personalized Instrument in order to cast an Effect with their Affinity Sphere receives -1 to the Difficulty on the Arete roll. So obviously that covers anything which only uses the Mind Sphere.<br /> <br /> But then I started pondering some ideas for Rotes that I've been working on, and I started to wonder how about how a Personalized Instrument might interact with Effects involving multiple Spheres. I'm going to use the Rotes as examples to help demonstrate my thoughts on different cases.<br /> <br /> (I'm also pretty inexperienced when it comes to designing Mage Effects, so let me know if I'm on the wrong track with anything!)<br /> <br /> So my first example would be a Correspondence 2 scrying spell which also includes Mind 1 to allow the Mage to pay full attention simultaneously to his everyday life and whatever is being observed by magic. In this case, the Mind Sphere is only serving to augment what is primarily a Correspondence Effect.<br /> <br /> My second example is a Correspondence 2 / Mind 2 &quot;Slipstream&quot;-type Effect which combines subtle warps of space and perception to increase the Difficulty of attack rolls, combining two different kinds of defence to make it still somewhat effective against an opponent who could resist either Effect on its own. In this case, you have two separate Spheres working towards a particular function, but using largely distinct methods of contributing to that outcome.<br /> <br /> If the Mage in question had Mind as their Affinity Sphere, would they receive a -1 Difficulty on their Arete roll for using a Personalized Instrument?<br /> <br /> The first example seems the most likely to be No, since you're just kind of &quot;splashing&quot; Mind in to beef up another Sphere's Effect.<br /> <br /> The second example seems more of a Maybe, since you do have a &quot;full&quot; Mind Effect as part of the function of the spell.<br /> <br /> My intuition is that it depends on whether or not the &quot;main&quot; Effect or function lies within the purview of the Affinity Sphere, but I feel like that could get messy. And, again, I have less experience with this stuff, so I figured I'd get some feedback.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you get -1 dif in Arete rolls when you use your affinity sphere. It doesn't matter how you use it, as long as Mind (in your examples) is on the effect, you get the bonus.<br /> <br /> Now, you must have a reason tocadd your affinity sphere. In your first example, Mind is improving the mage mental capabilities, so it's a sure bonus. In your second example I don't quite get what Mind is doing, do you care to explain further?<br /> <br /> Everytime you can fit in your sphere you get the bonus, but you can't juat say that you add it for no reason. As long as you can think at anything inside the raw to fit it, it's ok.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-11T22:46:39-08:00","id":1526691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1526281-personalized-instruments-and-conjunctional-sphere-effects?p=1526690#post1526690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, you get -1 dif in Arete rolls when you use your affinity sphere. It doesn't matter how you use it, as long as Mind (in your examples) is on the effect, you get the bonus.<br /> <br /> Now, you must have a reason tocadd your affinity sphere. In your first example, Mind is improving the mage mental capabilities, so it's a sure bonus. In your second example I don't quite get what Mind is doing, do you care to explain further?<br /> <br /> Everytime you can fit in your sphere you get the bonus, but you can't juat say that you add it for no reason. As long as you can think at anything inside the raw to fit it, it's ok.</div> </div> </div> </div>So in the second example, Mind 2 is being used to throw off the perceptions of any attackers, so that they *think* he's an inch or two further to the left/right/etc. than he actually is.<br /> <br /> Correspondence 2 would be used to make it so that he *actually* is an inch or so away from where they're actually targeting.<br /> <br /> The combination of the two is intended to insure that the spell retains some effectiveness against an opponent who can overcome or resist one of the effects, but not the other one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-12T03:36:52-08:00","id":1526698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1526281-personalized-instruments-and-conjunctional-sphere-effects?p=1526691#post1526691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So in the second example, Mind 2 is being used to throw off the perceptions of any attackers, so that they *think* he's an inch or two further to the left/right/etc. than he actually is.<br /> <br /> Correspondence 2 would be used to make it so that he *actually* is an inch or so away from where they're actually targeting.<br /> <br /> The combination of the two is intended to insure that the spell retains some effectiveness against an opponent who can overcome or resist one of the effects, but not the other one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aah, I see. Then yeah, the bonus would apply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T08:27:57-08:00","id":1526758,"title":"","content":"Really the main price of the personalized instrument is you have to use the personalized instrument and the personalized sphere to get that bonus, but what consequences that has are up in the air.<br /> <br /> The two unavoidable results of using the personalized sphere are that it gives opponents another sphere choice for countermagic and, if the personalized sphere needs a higher level than the other spheres, it increases the difficulty of casting.<br /> <br /> The rest depend on table rules and interpretations.<br /> <br /> For instance, there is a +1 penalty for casting with something that has the wrong resonance, and tools are listed as one of the things that can have the wrong resonance. I've always interpreted this as actual Resonance, but a gaming group could also apply that to using tools that are thematically inappropriate (e.g. healing a broken bone with a baseball bat). In that case the bonus from the personalized instrument would be cancelled out if it fits awkwardly into the spell.<br /> <br /> Likewise if the gaming group leans into the ability modifying magic rules, a player might have to make a more difficult ability roll for incorporating an odd personalized instrument into it, and even if there's no mechanical consequence, I'd still call using a tool in an odd situation is an opportunity for roleplaying.<br /> <br /> Whatever the case, I don't think there's an actual problem using the -1 difficulty for any spell the Mind sphere is used in as long as it actually has a real purpose in the spell. I'd only draw the line when it is only there to get the -1 bonus. I'd say try it out, see if any problems actually arise and adjust if necessary.<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T08:41:18-08:00","id":1526759,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the feedback everyone! I did wonder if this was just going to be one of the many things having to do with a Mage's Focus and casting Magic that just has to be left to Storyteller discretion, but I wanted to check in case people who had read the texts closer saw an answer I missed, or had considered this issue before.<br /> <br /> I suppose I might as well ask my follow-up question, since the consensus on the first matter seems to have been settled pretty quickly.<br /> <br /> In this example, the Personalized Instrument in question are Thought Forms. The idea is that he has a selection of Rote spells that he has created in advance, each one with an associated Thought Form to empower the Effect. So the first question that came to mind was this: would only a single Thought Form count as his Personalized Instrument, and thus he could only pick a *single* Mind spell for his casting bonus, or would having multiple Thought Forms for different spells all count as Personalized Instruments?<br /> <br /> (Since Thought Forms are an insanely flexible Instrument, I am imposing a couple of limits on myself. First of all, each of these Thought Forms would be &quot;embodied&quot; in a written text, and destroying the text would destroy the Thought Form until the Mage could recreate it. Secondly, there would be a limit to how many of these Thought Forms that he could keep handy.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}